course: dictionary
lesson: 9309
title: A word for a range
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A spectrum is a range of things that belong together, running from one end to the other. Look at the words around it to find out which kind of range is meant. «Use broad-spectrum sunscreen» means sunscreen that works against a wide range of harmful rays, not just one kind.
explain: In science, a spectrum is the band of colours that white light splits into. When you see a rainbow, you are looking at a spectrum. «Helium was discovered in the Sun's spectrum in 1868» tells you that scientists studied the colours of sunlight and found a new bright line among them.
explain: Spectrum can also mean a wide mix, as in «a wide spectrum of opinions», where people think many different things. The clues are wide and opinions, so the word means a big range of different ideas. Ask yourself: what is the range here, and what sits at each end?
explain: Be careful with «on the spectrum». Autism is a spectrum, so autistic people are all different from one another, with different strengths and needs. No two people are placed in exactly the same spot on it.
fact: A spectrum is a range of things, from one end to the other.
fact: «Spectrum» means the band of colours that white light splits into: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet.
fact: A prism splits white light into a spectrum, just as raindrops make a rainbow.
fact: «Broad-spectrum» means working against a wide range of things.
fact: Autism is a spectrum: autistic people are said to be "on the spectrum", and each one is different.
exercise: «Use broad-spectrum sunscreen of SPF 30 or more.» What does broad-spectrum suggest? | Works only on one small spot | *Works against a wide range | Smells of lemons | Is only for the beach
exercise: What colours are in the spectrum that white light splits into? | Brown and grey only | Pink and purple only | *Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet | Black and white only
exercise: «A wide spectrum of opinions» means | A kind of sunlight | One single opinion that everyone shares | A loud noise in the room | *A big range of different ideas
test: «Autistic people are on the spectrum, so each one is different.» What does this tell us? | Autistic people are all exactly the same | Autistic people cannot talk | *Autistic people differ from one another, across a range | Autism is a colour
test: What is the plural of spectrum, as in «more than one spectrum»? | *spectra or spectrums | spectrae only | spectrum-es | spectrums only
exam: Which word in «sunscreen of SPF 30 or more, broad-spectrum, goes on about 20 minutes before going out» tells you the sunscreen protects against many things? | summer | *broad-spectrum | minutes | sunscreen
